      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The variant and scope levers were good: county, state and nationwide, the Flinn spelling, and the Fl*n wildcard, each logged on its own. But the assessment of whether the nil is meaningful is unsound. The agent told the user the most likely cause is a severe transcription error, yet its bare nationwide search for Patrick Flynn also returned zero. A single mistranscribed entry cannot remove every Patrick Flynn from the index, so that zero points at the search or the collection, not at this one person. The rubric's pass bar asks for a correct assessment of what the absence means, and this one draws the wrong conclusion from its own evidence.\n"
